# Pass-15: PyInstaller build artifacts (cont.16-fup-6 -- bin\build_audit_exe.bat)
# Although the global `dist/` and `build/` patterns above already catch *most*
# PyInstaller outputs in any subdirectory, we add explicit `bin/`-anchored
# entries for archaeology clarity. `.spec` files SHOULD NOT be committed --
# they're rebuild-derived; the canonical build path is `bin\build_audit_exe.bat`.
/bin/dist/
/bin/build/
/bin/*.spec

# ComfyUI source files (TRACK -- never blanket-ignored anymore):
# - ComfyUI/tools/music_video_studio.py (operator-discoverable source)
# - ComfyUI/config/openrouter_free_models.txt (operator-discovery file)
# These land via the cont.17-fup-3 atomic-fix commit on 2026-07-11.
# Heavy-weight / generated subdirs remain excluded.
/ComfyUI/models/
/ComfyUI/custom_nodes/
/ComfyUI/output/
/ComfyUI/input/
/ComfyUI/.git/

# Surgical unblock (cont.17-fup-3 commit 3 rescue): negation for the blanket
# TOOLS/ (line 830) and [Cc]onfig/ (line 300) rules, which -- on Windows with
# core.ignorecase=true -- would otherwise block /ComfyUI/tools/ and
# /ComfyUI/config/ source files from beging tracked. These two negations let
# the existing blanket rules still cover other TOOLS/ + Config dirs in the repo.
!/ComfyUI/tools/
!/ComfyUI/config/

# Rescue-side backup from cont.17-fup-3 (rename, not rm -- preserves 90MB of
# upstream ComfyUI version metadata so the operator can `mv` it back if needed).
# Without this rule the 90MB would surface as `?? ComfyUI/_dot_git_bak_20260711/`
# in every git status; the name-specific /ComfyUI/.git/ rule does NOT match.
# (code-reviewer MUST-FIX landed as part of commit 4dbb29e00 amendment.)
/ComfyUI/_dot_git_bak_*/

# === Cont.17-fup-3 follow-up: explicit per-subdir + per-file deny rules for upstream-ComfyUI infra ===
# Why not just /ComfyUI/ blanket-denied: per gitignore "last matching pattern wins"
# semantics, a blanket /ComfyUI/ BEFORE the existing !/ComfyUI/tools/ + !/ComfyUI/config/
# negation rules would cascade-hide ALL children and override the negation
# ("git doesn't list excluded directories for performance reasons, so any
# patterns on contained files have no effect"). So we list each upstream-ComfyUI
# infra dir/file explicitly, AFTER the existing deny rules but BEFORE the new
# carve-out negation rules (below).
#
# Source-of-truth reference: `git status ComfyUI/` showed 92 untracked files
# after the cont.17-fup-3 source-file rescue unblocked tracking. The rules
# below suppress the 90+ upstream-ComfyUI infra files; the four blocks below
# re-include ONLY the operator-useful carve-outs (CLAUDE.md-referenced).

# Upstream-ComfyUI infra subdirs (no operator value)
/ComfyUI/.ci/
/ComfyUI/.github/
/ComfyUI/alembic_db/
/ComfyUI/api_server/
/ComfyUI/app/
/ComfyUI/blueprints/
/ComfyUI/comfy/
